IMPORT `cp1-div-b-maximum-earnings-and-exemption`

IMPORT `cp1-seat`

-- Worked cases for cp1-seat.l4: one or more per question, the facts a person in the seat would state. Every expected value was worked out by hand
-- from the text of the section (the layer-1 tests under cp1-tests-*.l4 give the arithmetic) before the file was run. The rates and maximums
-- are ILLUSTRATIVE 2024-style figures (employee base rate 4.95%, first additional 1%, second additional 4%; maximum pensionable earnings 68,500;
-- additional maximum 73,200; basic exemption 3,500; self-employed rates twice those). They are test inputs, not readings of Schedules 1 and 2 or of section 18.

§ `Cases -- Part I, Divisions A and B`

-- Which Minister is the Minister for Part I of the Plan
`cp1 seat case 1: Part I names the Minister of National Revenue` MEANS `Which Minister is the Minister for Part I of the Plan`
#ASSERT `cp1 seat case 1: Part I names the Minister of National Revenue` EQUALS `the Minister of National Revenue`

-- Does this officer's act under Part I count as an act of the Minister
`cp1 seat case 2: an authorized officer` MEANS `Does this officer's act under Part I count as an act of the Minister` WITH
    `the Minister has authorized the officer, or a class of officers that includes the officer, to act` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `cp1 seat case 2: an authorized officer` EQUALS TRUE

-- Does this officer's act under Part I count as an act of the Minister
`cp1 seat case 3: an officer the Minister has not authorized` MEANS `Does this officer's act under Part I count as an act of the Minister` WITH
    `the Minister has authorized the officer, or a class of officers that includes the officer, to act` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `cp1 seat case 3: an officer the Minister has not authorized` EQUALS FALSE

-- Is my employment pensionable employment
`cp1 seat case 4: an ordinary job in Canada` MEANS `Is my employment pensionable employment` WITH
    `my employment is in Canada` IS TRUE
    `my employment is under Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS FALSE
    `a regulation under section 7 includes my employment in pensionable employment` IS FALSE
    `a regulation under section 7 excepts my employment from pensionable employment` IS FALSE
    `my employment is in agriculture, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering` IS FALSE
    `the cash remuneration my employer pays me in the year` IS 40_000
    `my employer employs me on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration` IS TRUE
    `the working days in the year for which my employer so employs me` IS 200
    `my employment is of a casual nature` IS FALSE
    `my employment is for the purpose of my employer's trade or business` IS TRUE
    `I am a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada` IS FALSE
    `I am employed by my spouse or common-law partner` IS FALSE
    `my remuneration may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of my spouse or common-law partner` IS FALSE
    `I am a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty` IS FALSE
    `my remuneration is paid either directly or by me to the order` IS FALSE
    `no cash remuneration is paid to me` IS FALSE
    `I am the child of my employer` IS FALSE
    `I am maintained by my employer` IS FALSE
    `I am employed as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS FALSE
    `another Act of Parliament provides otherwise for my employment` IS FALSE
    `my employer employs persons in Canada` IS TRUE
    `a reciprocal agreement exempts my employer from the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act` IS FALSE
    `my employment is by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province` IS FALSE
    `my employment is by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization` IS FALSE
    `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS FALSE
    `my earnings from the employment are not included in computing my income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `cp1 seat case 4: an ordinary job in Canada` EQUALS TRUE

